// TEST: Log10 Dimensioned Operand (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3006
// log10 is a transcendental, so it takes the same unit rule as log/exp/sin:
// the series sums powers of the argument, which is meaningless once the
// argument carries a dimension. unitRulesForUnaryOp's OpMath catch-all is what
// applies it, so log10 inherited the rule by being added to
// Grad.mathIntrinsics -- this pins that the catch-all really does cover a name
// it was not written for. Divide by a reference quantity first.
Unit meters
let d: Float<meters> = 100.0
let bad = log10(d)
